# EXP-004 smoke (before the spec commit, seeds 100-102 = outside the registered seeds 0-29): does `--enforcer-share 100` hold the institution world's composition, and does the rule arm survive?
date: 2026-10-18 JST (M1, 8 cores, 16 GB, macOS 26.6.2, rustc 1.99.1, release build of the working tree that added enforcer_share_permille / --blind / --signal-radius / --memory-slots and the sweep's 4-6 columns)
note: the first attempt at the `le` arm (not shown) passed "--enact encroach" as one zsh word and so ran without the rule; this is the corrected run from a sh script. The composition and E_L readings of both arms were seen before the predictions of EXP-004 were fixed (disclosed in the spec).
